{"thought": null, "tool": "commit_pick", "arguments": {"candidate": "9", "rationale": "All candidates have GDS 0, so this score does not distinguish density. Pick S4 at 270°: NHR -0.441 is best, IWR 0.704 is near-best, and LLC 0.690 is tied for best. Its LFR -0.248 is a meaningful void cost, but its right-side position uses the lower part of the skyline and leaves S1, S14 and S17 for later. Their future feasibility and final-wall effects are not known.

The strongest flush, high-load alternatives are S4 180° (6: NHR -1.037, IWR 0.378, LLC 0.690, LFR -0.084) and S17 180° (7: -1.036, 0.180, 0.690, -0.092). They place broad stones on the higher left portion; 7 preserves S4 but has weaker interlocking. S4 0° (1: -0.907, 0.701, 0.690, -0.264) has similarly good interlocking and load to 9 but worse course-height score and a slightly worse void score. S14 0° (2: -1.032, 0.266, 0.172, -0.045) is the most flush and places the otherwise single-option S14, but has much lower load and raises the left edge.

Other options: S1 0° (0: -0.976, 0.092, 0.690, -0.103) is relatively flush and strong but poorly interlocked; S1 90° (3: -0.533, 0.388, 0.690, -0.323) and 270° (8: -0.467, 0.573, 0.345, -0.282) work on the right but trade interlocking, load and void against 9; S1 180° (5: -1.049, 0.237, 0.345, -0.059) is flush but weak in load and course height. S4 90° (4: -0.946, 0.777, 0.172, -0.498) has the best interlocking but the worst void and low load. S17 270° (10: -0.603, 0.353, 0.517, -0.358) uses the right side but is worse than 9 on each of these four scores. Choosing any S1 or S17 option preserves S4, while 9 consumes S4; the listed current poses do not establish which stones will remain placeable afterward."}}

